     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica\">Dear listfolk,</span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><font color=\"#000000\"><font face=\"Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">We would like to draw your attention to the below report, which may be of interest to the distance sampling community:</span></font></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica;font-size:10pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Bouchet PJ, Miller DL, Roberts JJ, Mannocci L, Harris CM and Thomas L (2019). From here and now to there and then: Practical recommendations for extrapolating cetacean density surface models to novel conditions. CREEM Technical Report 2019-01, 59p.</span><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica\"> </span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica\">The report summarises current approaches to extrapolation detection and diagnosis, with a strong emphasis on spatial models of cetacean density/abundance such as those typically resulting from line transect surveys, and implemented in the dsm R package. </span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica\">This work is an output from the Living Marine Resources (LMR)-funded DenMod project, and is a collaboration between the University of St Andrews, Duke University, and the University of Montpellier.</span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica\"> </span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica\">You can read the report freely here:<span> </span></span><a href=\"https://research-repository.st-andrews.ac.uk/handle/10023/18509\" style=\"text-decoration-line:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://research-repository.st-andrews.ac.uk/handle/10023/18509&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473882075000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Twh1H-suD6ilj8DV4Au2k\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica\">https://research-repository.st-andrews.ac.uk/handle/10023/18509</span></a><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica\">.</span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica\"> </span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica\">In addition, relevant R code for extrapolation assessments can be downloaded from our Github site.</span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#000000\"><a href=\"https://densitymodelling.github.io/model-extrapolation/\" style=\"text-decoration-line:underline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://densitymodelling.github.io/model-extrapolation/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473882075000&amp;usg=AOvVaw06yNf1mfOj_qJTfApa61s_\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica\">https://densitymodelling.github.io/model-extrapolation/</span></a><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica\"> </span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica\">Note that a standalone R package is currently being developed to capture the methods described in the report (and more). </span></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica\">Future releases/updates will be announced on this list.</span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica\"> </span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><font color=\"#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica\">Best wishes,</span><u></u><u></u></font></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:Helvetica\"><font color=\"#000000\">Phil</font></span></p></div>"
